   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 695 of the laws of 1994 amending the civil service law\nrelating to injunctive relief in improper practice cases, in relation to\nextending the effectiveness of provisions contained therein",
    "basePrintNo": "S5831",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5831-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 695 of 1994",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5831\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 695 of the laws of 1994 amend-\ning the civil service law relating to injunctive relief in improper\npractice cases, in relation to extending the effectiveness of provisions\ncontained therein\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo continue to provide public employees with an expedited method to\nreceive injunctive relief for improper labor practices.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends chapter 695 of the laws of 1994 amending\nthe civil service law to extend from June 30, 2019 to June 30, 2021 the\nprovisions allowing a public employee to petition before the Public\nEmployment Relations Board or the New York City Board of Collective\nBargaining and receive injunctive relief for an improper practice\ncharge.\n\nSection two of the bill sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nInjunctive relief was enacted in 1994 to provide an expedited method to\nresolve improper practice cases in the public sector where there was\ndeemed to be immediate and irreparable harm. Since it took effect in\n1995, it has enabled labor and management to resolve numerous issues. It\nis, therefore, appropriate that this law be extended.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017: S6477 - chaptered\n2015: S4932 - chaptered\n2013: S4909 - chaptered\n2011: S4131 - chaptered\n2009: S1407 - chaptered\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
